Marks the nodes an extension's content script makes, for the core's agent (//browser_core/
agent_page.cc): Blink sets a node's last free flag when it's made while script runs in an
extension's isolated world, as a password manager's in-page button and menu are. DevTools'
accessibility tree gives such a node, and every node inside it, the property fromExtension, and an
accessibility snapshot, which the core's read of a page takes, the HTML attribute fromExtension. An
agent's outline and text leave them out, and the core refuses an agent's click that would land on
one, so an agent never acts on an extension's controls as if they were the page's (#2355). Only a
node made while script runs is checked, and only once a world other than the page's exists; the
parser's never are.

